   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to requiring the\ndepartment of agriculture and markets to develop and maintain a database of\nNew York state farms and farm products",
    "basePrintNo": "S6330",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6330-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §16, Ag & Mkts L",
    "lawSection": "Agriculture and Markets Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6330\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the agriculture and markets law, in relation to requir-\ning the department of agriculture and markets to develop and maintain a\ndatabase of New York state farms and farm products\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo require the department to establish a database of New York state\nfarms and farm products\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends the agriculture and markets law in relation to devel-\noping and maintaining a publicly available searchable database of New\nYork state farms and farm products.\n\nSection two states the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAgriculture is a $3.6 billion industry in New York State. With over\n35,000 farms, New York is a leading producer of some of the nation's\nbest food and beverages. Despite the various products grown across the\nstate, there is currently no centralized way to access this information.\n\nA database will connect consumers to producers of farm products while\nstrengthening the supply chain across New York. This will allow restau-\nrants and other entities easy access to the array of products farms\nacross New York State have available. Purchasing directly from local\nfarmers will assist not only in strengthening our agricultural sector,\nbut also in bettering New York State's environment, vibrant communities\nand small businesses, and strong local economies.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the one hundred eightieth day after it\nshall become a law.\n",
